WEBVTT

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.660
"This is a work of fiction. The characters,
organizations, and names herein are fictitious,
and bear no relation to existing entities."

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:40.540
Until then, in Ikebukuro,
the G-Boys called all the shots

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:45.830
for the delinquents, dancers,
thrashers, and tons of other kids.

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:49.450
Their King is Takashi Andou.

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:54.000
A cool ruler, not unlike a glass
placed inside a freezer.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.660
The object of adoration for this town's girls.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:00.160
And then, <i>he </i>showed up.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:04.620
He suddenly started dancing in West Gate Park
when it was packed with kids,

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:09.080
and in the blink of an eye,
he won over everybody there.

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:15.040
His name is Kyouichi Ozaki.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:19.410
Another bit of charisma
that landed in Ikebukuro.

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:32.250
"Ikebukuro West Gate Park"

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:53.750
"OK Curry"

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:56.750
"OK Curry"

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:56.750
OK Curry is currently running a promotion!

00:02:56.750 --> 00:03:01.660
We sure are! Get free extra rice
with your OK Fried Rice!

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:04.370
All together now! How much is OK Curry?

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:06.160
2-9! 2-9!

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:07.790
¥290!

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:09.290
How much is OK Fried Rice?

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:10.910
3-2! 3-2!

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:13.250
¥320!

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:15.700
You're not cut out for our company!

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:17.830
If you want to quit, just get it over with!

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:20.580
I'm sorry! I'll work harder from now on!

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:23.120
Not from now on! Right now!

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:26.580
Our company doesn't need
someone who can't do it now!

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:29.000
You're nothing but garbage!

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:31.200
I'm sorry! I really am!

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:32.700
Twenty push-ups!

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:35.910
Yes, sir! I'd be glad to!

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:37.540
One!

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:39.410
Two!

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:41.000
Three!

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:46.660
Welcome! We hope you enjoy
your meal at OK Curry!

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:48.250
Thank you very much!

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:50.950
We do hope you'll come again!

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:52.870
Thank you for waiting!

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:54.580
Please, take your time!

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:55.160
"OK Curry"          "Now hiring"

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:57.290
"OK Curry"          "Now hiring"

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:57.290
This is the place, Makoto.

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:04.290
The rumors were true,
and maybe then some. Wow...

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:08.120
How does it taste?

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:11.700
It's not bad. But it's not good either.

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:15.290
You can eat your fill for a very low price.

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:19.000
It's quite the typical business
approach in today's world.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:23.330
Behind it are young people working for low pay.

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:26.250
There are many who're made
to work so much, they lose sleep,

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:30.040
and their physical and mental
health suffer as a result.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:32.660
Not that it's been made all that public yet.

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:36.330
And you're saying the Red Angels are involved?

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:37.790
King?!

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:40.620
Makoto-san!

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:41.790
Masaru.

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:44.500
You've been working here, too?

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:48.450
The one who was doing push-ups
is a schoolmate of mine.

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:51.620
His name's Mitsuki,
and he was just recently hired.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:55.450
What did he do wrong?
Was it worth that kind of reprimand?

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:58.080
He got there five minutes late, that's all.

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:02.700
But this is his first food service job,
so he's pretty clumsy.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:05.500
That's why the MPs watch him closely.

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:11.370
They're called Military Police, and they go
from shop to shop, shaking things up.

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:16.410
In addition to Masaru, about
20 G-Boys are working for OK.

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:21.950
But recently, I've received numerous reports
of excessively horrible treatment.

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:26.750
We hear some employees
get angry enough to fight back.

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:31.620
But when talk turns to accusations
and lawsuits, it's not the MPs...

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:37.450
Some shadowy group of violent punks
shows up out of nowhere and issues threats.

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:40.200
Masaru has actually seen them in action.

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:44.000
A violent group belonging to Kyouichi Ozaki?

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:46.580
The Red Angels, apparently.

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:52.950
Kyouichi Ozaki just recently appeared
in Ikebukuro, and rapidly built up his group.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:56.040
They say he's an amazing dancer.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:59.620
This is another rumor,
but to join the Red Angels,

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:03.700
it seems there's some ceremony,
like it's a religious group or a secret society.

00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:06.160
For my part, I don't intend to compete,

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:09.950
even if there's a new group
of kids besides the G-Boys.

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:14.580
Everyone should do as they
see fit. That's Ikebukuro.

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:22.540
But if they join up with a sweatshop
and harm the G-Boys, that changes things.

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:25.000
But there's no definite proof yet, right?

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:28.290
That's why I want you to find out the truth.

00:06:28.290 --> 00:06:33.160
Whether it's the Red Angels
who are OK Holdings' goon squad.

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:38.000
I haven't seen their faces.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:42.830
About ten days ago, I was walking
home with another coworker.

00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:45.750
He was super pissed about the place's practices.

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:49.290
He said he'd sue for overtime pay, if he had to.

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:52.120
We parted ways at one point.

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:53.120
And then...

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:56.580
You ungrateful punk!

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:58.580
When I ran back in surprise...

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:05.540
He quit his job after that.

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:08.080
Looks like he never filed a lawsuit, either.

00:07:09.910 --> 00:07:13.120
There's no proof that was the company's doing.

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:17.080
It was declared an unrelated
random attack, and that was that.

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:20.330
What about the story that they're Red Angels?

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:23.500
That's a rumor going around in the G-Boys.

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:28.540
The truth is, I'm reluctant
to go against the company.

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:30.700
Although it makes me feel bad for King.

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:33.950
Why? Because you'll be targeted, too?

00:07:33.950 --> 00:07:36.450
There is that...

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:39.910
But I used to be such a dumb troublemaker.

00:07:39.910 --> 00:07:42.910
I worried my parents so much.

00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:47.290
But as I got older, I figured
I couldn't keep on doing that stuff.

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:55.000
So, I came to Ikebukuro, got into
the G-Boys, and got a job, too.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:58.370
My parents are unbelievably happy.

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:01.660
Because I've finally started working for real.

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:04.080
I've tried hard to get this far.

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:06.450
I'd like to keep on going.

00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:10.200
I think Mitsuki and the others
feel the same way.

00:08:12.870 --> 00:08:15.580
Makoto-san, are you really going?

00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:18.080
I'll go check them out, at least.

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:21.290
These Red Angels of Kyouichi Ozaki's.

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:33.000
Wh-What's with these guys?!

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:35.080
Why're they all up in our faces?!

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:36.500
Who knows?

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:38.330
Stay close to me.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:45.450
Wait! Wait! Wait!

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:49.660
Don't go doing whatever you want
when Kyouichi isn't around!

00:08:49.660 --> 00:08:51.910
You must be Makoto Majima-san?

00:08:51.910 --> 00:08:54.750
Takashi Andou-san's friend?

00:08:54.750 --> 00:08:57.620
I hear you're famous in Ikebukuro.

00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:58.750
Are you here on business?

00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:01.330
I wouldn't use that word for it.

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:04.040
I heard an amazing dancer had shown up,

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:07.080
so I wondered what he was like, and I dropped by.

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:09.200
Kyouichi isn't here today.

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:11.660
I can pass on a message, if you like.

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:14.910
No, I'll come back.

00:09:14.910 --> 00:09:17.750
Hey, is his dancing <i>that </i>great?

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:21.580
Yes! I'm sure it would surprise you.

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:29.540
We made it back alive...

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:32.250
So, did anyone there look like the culprits?

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:34.330
Like, the look in their eyes, or their build?

00:09:34.330 --> 00:09:36.620
Well, I'm not so sure.

00:09:36.620 --> 00:09:37.660
There's a jumper!

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:38.700
It's a suicide!

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:42.000
I heard a young guy from OK Curry is gonna jump!

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:49.250
Hold it right there! Let's talk about this!

00:09:49.250 --> 00:09:51.540
There's no point in going on living!

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:54.500
I'm not cut out for society or my company!

00:09:54.500 --> 00:09:56.370
There's no place for me!

00:09:56.370 --> 00:09:57.870
Mitsuki!

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:01.370
Let me have that!

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:02.370
Makoto?!

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:05.660
This guy's his coworker
and his home-town schoolmate!

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:07.580
Wh-What do I do?!

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:11.500
Anything. Talk to him, and get him to back down!

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:17.000
Mitsuki!

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:19.200
Mitsuki, can you hear me?!

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:22.120
I'm really sorry! It's my fault!

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:25.660
This happened because I invited you!

00:10:25.660 --> 00:10:27.620
It's not your fault, Masaru-san!

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:30.580
It's because I suck at working
and communicating!

00:10:30.580 --> 00:10:34.000
Don't sweat the company! Just quit!

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:35.950
There's no reason to die!

00:10:35.950 --> 00:10:38.410
If I quit, they'll get me
for breach of contract!

00:10:38.410 --> 00:10:42.290
I can't cause any more trouble for my family!

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:44.870
There's no need to pay money for that!

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:48.120
Come on, let's you and me start over again!

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:50.540
If you quit, I will, too!

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:53.870
You're not a worthless person!

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:55.660
Masaru-san...

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:03.250
I'm sorry, Masaru-san!

00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:09.330
I'm not about to cause trouble for you, too.

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:22.620
Are you all right?!

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:23.540
Are you hurt?!

00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:25.250
He needs an ambulance, now!

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:30.000
"Episode 2"

00:11:32.660 --> 00:11:35.200
Looks like he'll make it.

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:37.580
Go visit him in the hospital tomorrow.

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:42.790
Makoto-san, I've made up my mind.

00:11:42.790 --> 00:11:44.790
It's vengeance for Mitsuki.

00:11:44.790 --> 00:11:47.370
I'll take them to court
or do whatever I have to,

00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:50.750
to get them to pay for overtime,
or medical fees!

00:11:50.750 --> 00:11:53.450
Before there's another case like Mitsuki's.

00:11:53.830 --> 00:11:56.580
"Majima Produce"

00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:59.660
Makoto? Masaru was attacked.

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:04.000
It was a masked gang of five.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:06.750
It apparently happened on his way home.

00:12:06.750 --> 00:12:09.290
We received word two hours ago.

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:12.540
He said that was the soonest
he was able to use a phone.

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:15.660
Then he can talk to us, at least.

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:21.870
Maybe we should have attacked
the Red Angels first.

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:24.870
"Hospital"

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:24.870
I'm sorry you had to come here, King.

00:12:24.870 --> 00:12:26.830
You, too, Makoto-san and Hiroto-san.

00:12:26.830 --> 00:12:28.450
You had a rough night, Masaru.

00:12:28.450 --> 00:12:31.200
Don't talk too much. It won't help you heal.

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:32.950
I'm fine!

00:12:32.950 --> 00:12:37.660
I've got some broken bones,
but they should discharge me soon.

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:40.910
Mitsuki's injuries were lighter
than we thought, too.

00:12:40.910 --> 00:12:43.700
Masaru-san, who are these guys?

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:46.830
It's King, of my G-Boys group.

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:51.000
I can't believe you came to visit me personally!

00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:58.370
Until just before that day,
I had never even considered dying.

00:12:58.370 --> 00:13:02.410
But I figured I'd probably keep
getting yelled at every day,

00:13:02.410 --> 00:13:06.660
and even if I got another job,
my whole life would be like that.

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:08.790
Once that thought hit me...

00:13:08.790 --> 00:13:13.120
I don't think you're unimportant, Mitsuki.

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:19.540
I know! King! Could we let him join the G-Boys?

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:22.250
He's a little unreliable, but he's a great guy!

00:13:22.250 --> 00:13:24.870
Uh, no, I...

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:40.910
Kyouichi Ozaki!

00:13:57.500 --> 00:14:01.040
Kyouichi, this is a hospital...

00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:03.370
Hi!

00:14:03.370 --> 00:14:06.200
Sorry for showing up uninvited yesterday!

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:09.580
What, are you here to visit someone, too?

00:14:09.580 --> 00:14:11.580
What a coincidence!

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:15.700
M-Makoto-san! That's right! A real coincidence!

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:18.500
Talk about surprising!

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:23.120
Remember, Kyouichi? I told you
yesterday. Makoto Majima-san.

00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:28.200
He went<i> out of his way </i>to come see you.

00:14:29.870 --> 00:14:33.870
Sorry I wasn't there
after you came all that way.

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:39.040
So, you're Takashi Andou? Ikebukuro's King?

00:14:39.040 --> 00:14:43.040
Kyouichi Ozaki, huh? Who are you here to see?

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:45.700
Mitsuki Fujimoto, there.

00:14:45.700 --> 00:14:49.080
He only just joined,
but he's one of our members.

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:50.000
Huh?!

00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:51.120
For real, Mitsuki?!

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:53.620
Yes. I was thinking of telling you...

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:55.790
Don't sit on info like that!

00:14:55.790 --> 00:15:00.580
Well, you never told me you
were in the G-Boys, Masaru-san!

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:03.870
That's not something
I can casually tell an outsider!

00:15:05.870 --> 00:15:08.910
You came to see one of
your guys in the hospital.

00:15:08.910 --> 00:15:11.080
Your sense of duty surprises me.

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:12.830
Aren't you doing the same thing?

00:15:12.830 --> 00:15:14.080
"Nao"

00:15:14.450 --> 00:15:16.750
In other words, it's like this?

00:15:16.750 --> 00:15:20.580
We think it's the Red Angels,
and you think it's the G-Boys

00:15:20.580 --> 00:15:25.250
who're working for OK Holdings
and hassling each other's guys.

00:15:25.250 --> 00:15:31.370
Yes. We heard OK Holdings had hired
young Ikebukuro gang members.

00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:34.540
So naturally, we figured it meant the G-Boys.

00:15:34.540 --> 00:15:36.160
Same for us.

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:40.750
If it wasn't us, it inevitably
had to be the Red Angels.

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:44.750
We, too, have many members
who work for OK Holdings.

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:49.540
It looks like the company must
have deliberately spread that rumor.

00:15:50.790 --> 00:15:55.450
They make the G-Boys believe the Red Angels
are in league with the company.

00:15:55.450 --> 00:16:00.120
They make the Red Angels believe the G-Boys
are in league with the company.

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:04.330
That way, they make the troublemakers
keep each other in check.

00:16:04.330 --> 00:16:07.370
Then, neither of them can easily interfere.

00:16:07.370 --> 00:16:11.370
The company can take advantage
of that to do as they please.

00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:14.080
And it's no big deal if we figure it out.

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:16.290
After all, we're just kids.

00:16:16.290 --> 00:16:19.830
Or, that's probably how they see it.

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:22.000
We've been underestimated.

00:16:28.120 --> 00:16:30.910
I'm Makoto Majima, with Monthly Street Beat.

00:16:30.910 --> 00:16:34.580
"OK Holdings Press Conference"

00:16:30.910 --> 00:16:34.580
Yes, sir, go right in.

00:16:34.580 --> 00:16:38.290
Makoto-san, why do you have
a magazine's business card?

00:16:38.290 --> 00:16:41.290
I write a column for them on the side.

00:16:41.290 --> 00:16:43.250
It's pretty popular.

00:16:43.250 --> 00:16:44.910
Huh...

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:54.370
The other day, an employee of our
OK Holdings attempted suicide in Ikebukuro.

00:16:54.370 --> 00:16:58.750
We would like to extend to him
our heartfelt sympathy.

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:04.410
There are increasing calls online

00:17:04.410 --> 00:17:07.790
to condemn OK Holdings
for other incidents as well.

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:11.370
It is indeed true that there is an ongoing
series of unfortunate incidents.

00:17:11.370 --> 00:17:13.870
However, we believe there is nothing illegal

00:17:13.870 --> 00:17:17.000
about our company's working conditions.

00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:20.790
There's word that some young people
have, in fact, lost their lives.

00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:23.500
For the sake of our employees
working happily every day,

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:28.700
I'd like to state this loud and clear:

00:17:28.700 --> 00:17:31.790
Ours is a good company!

00:17:33.250 --> 00:17:38.160
Regarding the employees who lost their lives,
we offer our sincerest condolences.

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:43.700
We are considering affixing their names
to a school we plan to establish in Africa.

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:45.500
You're going to turn an employee's suicide

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:47.500
into a heroic tale for company publicity?!

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:48.660
President Ohki.

00:17:48.660 --> 00:17:53.830
I have here someone who submitted
his letter of resignation to OK Holdings.

00:17:53.830 --> 00:17:55.790
His name is Masaru Taniguchi-kun,

00:17:55.790 --> 00:17:59.830
and he's a friend of the employee
who recently attempted suicide.

00:17:59.830 --> 00:18:04.830
He himself is also a victim, as he was
attacked around the time he quit.

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:09.160
He's already contacted an attorney,
and a lawsuit is being prepared.

00:18:09.160 --> 00:18:14.450
President Ohki, do you have
anything to say to him?

00:18:14.450 --> 00:18:17.540
Yes, everything we said is true.

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:27.910
And after how badly we beat you the other day?

00:18:27.910 --> 00:18:29.830
Looks like you haven't learned.

00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:38.200
Ingrates who cause problems for the place
that looked after them never live long.

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:44.160
For the record, we know the names
of your family, and where they live.

00:18:44.160 --> 00:18:48.080
You know, that's like admitting
you have ties to the company.

00:18:52.750 --> 00:18:58.700
Yamamoto. Tsuzuki. Kamioka.
Kagashima. Kimimoto.

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:02.580
Five guys too rotten to get into any group.

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:05.580
Getting info on you was easy enough.

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:08.830
We have a lot more people, after all.

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:12.160
Andou, huh? You've always
got your minions with you.

00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:14.580
Can't win a fight on your own?

00:19:14.580 --> 00:19:18.750
I suppose I'll fight five of you guys in a row.

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:21.830
Not that I like punching rotten meat.

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:31.290
Leave Andou to me.
I've always wanted to fight him.

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:39.160
Then I'll take Muscles over there.

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:54.370
Die!

00:19:58.540 --> 00:19:59.790
That idiot.

00:20:17.870 --> 00:20:20.700
What's wrong?! You're all talk, after all?!

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:39.450
Kyouichi-san!

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:44.000
Asshole!

00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:45.040
Mitsuki!

00:20:54.540 --> 00:20:56.950
That was pretty good. What do you say?

00:20:56.950 --> 00:21:01.410
Want to quit the Red Angels, and join us?

00:21:01.410 --> 00:21:03.540
I wish you'd stop joking.

00:21:03.540 --> 00:21:06.790
Mitsuki is an important part of our group.

00:21:06.790 --> 00:21:08.200
Right?

00:21:16.910 --> 00:21:19.040
What are you looking at, Makoto-san?

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:22.450
"OK Holdings employees arrested
on suspicion of assault and intimidation"

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:22.450
The OK Holdings MPs got caught.

00:21:22.450 --> 00:21:25.370
"OK Holdings employees arrested
on suspicion of assault and intimidation"

00:21:22.450 --> 00:21:25.370
For using those five guys
for assault and intimidation.

00:21:25.370 --> 00:21:25.910
"Rabbit"

00:21:25.910 --> 00:21:27.250
"Rabbit"

00:21:25.910 --> 00:21:27.250
What about the president?

00:21:27.250 --> 00:21:29.040
"Rabbit"

00:21:27.250 --> 00:21:29.040
Hospitalized for sudden illness.

00:21:29.040 --> 00:21:33.700
"Rabbit"

00:21:29.040 --> 00:21:33.700
But he's got the lawsuit,
so I don't suppose he can run forever.

00:21:33.700 --> 00:21:37.450
I hear the G-Boys arranged
for the lawsuit attorney.

00:21:37.450 --> 00:21:40.910
They have a lot of alums.
That means lots of connections.

00:21:40.910 --> 00:21:44.250
Impressive. We'd better take notes.

00:21:44.250 --> 00:21:46.290
Hey, what's your name?

00:21:46.290 --> 00:21:49.200
Isogai. Tomomi Isogai.

00:21:49.200 --> 00:21:52.790
I'm what you'd call an
Archangel of the Red Angels.

00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:55.080
Oh, yes, Makoto-san.

00:21:55.080 --> 00:21:57.160
Kyouichi asked me to give this to you.

00:21:57.160 --> 00:22:02.000
With this, you can come and go
freely at Red Angels gatherings.

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:05.040
Oh, okay. Thanks.

00:22:07.160 --> 00:22:09.750
Thus did the G-Boys and Red Angels

00:22:09.750 --> 00:22:12.750
set up respective bases
at the West and East Gates,

00:22:12.750 --> 00:22:16.120
and decide to coexist in Ikebukuro.

00:22:16.120 --> 00:22:18.750
Although there's still a bit of tension.

00:22:19.160 --> 00:22:20.000
<i>What's up</i>

00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:23.120
<i>A world where guys with plans</i>
<i>are the first to fade away</i>

00:22:23.120 --> 00:22:25.830
<i>The thought hit me after being out all night</i>

00:22:25.830 --> 00:22:28.660
<i>A gulf forms with the respectable types</i>

00:22:28.660 --> 00:22:31.790
<i>The MIC you nervously gripped</i>

00:22:31.790 --> 00:22:34.410
<i>Leave it behind on the stage</i>

00:22:34.410 --> 00:22:37.500
<i>Unable to trust in the next move</i>

00:22:37.500 --> 00:22:40.450
<i>You get down off the stage of dreams</i>

00:22:40.450 --> 00:22:43.250
<i>Fade away from the bustle of the scene</i>

00:22:43.250 --> 00:22:46.160
<i>Do you know what becomes of him after that?</i>

00:22:46.160 --> 00:22:49.290
<i>In fact, are you even prepared to know?</i>

00:22:49.290 --> 00:22:52.040
<i>Now that we're involved,</i>
<i>I want to watch you take off</i>

00:22:52.040 --> 00:22:54.790
<i>From the runway you chose</i>

00:22:54.790 --> 00:22:58.790
<i>If we happen to meet again today or tomorrow</i>

00:22:58.790 --> 00:23:02.450
<i>Somewhere on this Earth</i>

00:23:02.450 --> 00:23:03.910
<i>Let's have fun freestyling</i>

00:23:03.910 --> 00:23:07.000
<i>Like we did that time</i>

00:23:08.830 --> 00:23:09.660
<i>What's up</i>

00:23:09.660 --> 00:23:11.160
<i>After the live show</i>

00:23:11.160 --> 00:23:12.660
<i>In a train window</i>

00:23:12.660 --> 00:23:14.040
<i>A brother's face, I find</i>

00:23:14.040 --> 00:23:15.540
<i>Comes suddenly to mind</i>

00:23:15.540 --> 00:23:18.540
<i>Right now, I don't feel like</i>
<i>lookin' back on the past</i>

00:23:18.540 --> 00:23:21.410
<i>But no way in hell am I forgettin' it</i>

00:23:21.410 --> 00:23:22.870
<i>After the live show</i>

00:23:22.870 --> 00:23:24.370
<i>In a train window</i>

00:23:24.370 --> 00:23:25.790
<i>A brother's face, I find</i>

00:23:25.790 --> 00:23:27.250
<i>Comes suddenly to mind</i>

00:23:27.250 --> 00:23:30.160
<i>Right now, I don't feel like</i>
